Work with your Redmine issues without leaving the browser.

Redmine Helper puts the issues assigned to you — and the ones you watch — in
Chrome's side panel, right next to whatever you are working on. It tells you when
something changes, and lets you act on it without opening Redmine.

- Search your issues, and see at a glance which have changed since you last looked
- Edit status, tracker, priority, assignee, % done and estimated hours in place
- Read the full issue history, add comments, and attach files
- Track time on an issue and log it straight to Redmine, with unsent sessions
  queued locally so nothing is lost
- Create an issue from text selected on any page, via the right-click menu
- Optional desktop notifications for new or updated issues
- Browse projects and news, and work in a wide full-page view when you want one
- Dark mode

Requires Redmine 5.0 or later with the REST API enabled (Administration →
Settings → API). After installing, open the options page and enter your Redmine
URL and API access key, which you will find on your Redmine account page.

Everything stays in your browser. The extension talks only to the Redmine host
you configure and sends nothing anywhere else. Access is requested for that one
host rather than for every site you visit.
